WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.321
Narrator: Good morning, Chad.

2
00:00:01.321 --> 00:00:06.257
Narrator: It's Wednesday, November twenty-fifth, and this is your Daily Briefing.

3
00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:08.691
Narrator: Here's what you need to know today.

4
00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.697
Narrator: Let's start at home with the weather.

5
00:00:11.697 --> 00:00:15.081
Narrator: The first freeze of the season arrived overnight.

6
00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:29.173
Narrator: The National Weather Service in Fort Worth has a freeze warning for Tarrant, Denton, and Collin counties until nine this morning, with lows as cold as twenty-five degrees in the western parts of the area.

7
00:00:29.173 --> 00:00:33.180
Narrator: In north Fort Worth, expect a low right around thirty-one.

8
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:38.360
Narrator: If you have pipes, plants, or pets outside, check on them before you leave.

9
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.753
Narrator: Today will be sunny and cool, with a high near fifty-two.

10
00:00:42.753 --> 00:00:51.469
Narrator: Thanksgiving looks about the same: clear skies, a high in the low fifties, and another light freeze possible Thursday morning.

11
00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:53.060
Narrator: Then a warm-up arrives.

12
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:57.971
Narrator: Friday climbs into the mid sixties, and Saturday gets close to seventy.

13
00:00:58.421 --> 00:01:03.591
Narrator: In local news, the Thanksgiving week holiday kickoff is happening downtown.

14
00:01:03.591 --> 00:01:11.519
Narrator: Sundance Square's Christmas tree, billed as the tallest live Christmas tree in Texas, is set to light up this week.

15
00:01:11.519 --> 00:01:17.034
Narrator: It's an easy outing if you're looking for something to do over the long weekend.

16
00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:19.537
Narrator: Now to the national headlines.

17
00:01:19.987 --> 00:01:24.192
Narrator: The biggest business and political story right now is Nvidia.

18
00:01:24.192 --> 00:01:31.775
Narrator: The company's board reinstated Jensen Huang as chief executive on Monday, only days after saying it would not.

19
00:01:31.775 --> 00:01:39.289
Narrator: Huang had resigned after admitting to an affair with a woman suspected of being a Chinese intelligence asset.

20
00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:52.800
Narrator: President Trump says he personally helped broker Huang's return, and Senate Democrats say they will open an investigation into the White House's role once they take control of Congress in January.

21
00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:58.660
Narrator: Separately, Reuters reports the S.E.C. is looking into Nvidia's accounting practices.

22
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:06.725
Narrator: The company has formed a new national security and export control committee and is hiring a chief compliance officer.

23
00:02:07.175 --> 00:02:10.612
Narrator: Second, if you're traveling this week, plan ahead.

24
00:02:10.612 --> 00:02:22.709
Narrator: The Federal Aviation Administration says this will be the busiest Thanksgiving travel period in sixteen years, with more than four hundred seventeen thousand flights scheduled.

25
00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:30.926
Narrator: Third, on trade, the United States is reportedly preparing to raise tariffs on China and several other countries.

26
00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:38.624
Narrator: Details are still emerging, so watch for the specifics, especially if any of your clients buy hardware overseas.

27
00:02:39.074 --> 00:02:40.990
Narrator: Now let's go to the markets.

28
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.133
Narrator: Tuesday was a split day on Wall Street.

29
00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:52.006
Narrator: The Dow rose eight tenths of a percent, gaining about four hundred twenty points, and closed above fifty thousand.

30
00:02:52.006 --> 00:03:01.606
Narrator: Meanwhile, the S and P five hundred fell half a percent to about seventy-two hundred, and the Nasdaq dropped nearly one and a half percent.

31
00:03:01.606 --> 00:03:07.545
Narrator: The story was a rotation out of A.I. chip stocks and into health care and value names.

32
00:03:07.545 --> 00:03:15.625
Narrator: Nvidia gave back almost six percent after Monday's big rally on the Huang news, and Micron fell about eleven percent.

33
00:03:15.625 --> 00:03:20.390
Narrator: On the upside, Sanofi agreed to buy Insmed, which lifted health care.

34
00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:26.467
Narrator: Kohl's jumped about nineteen percent and Dollar Tree about eleven after strong earnings.

35
00:03:26.917 --> 00:03:39.231
Narrator: On the economy, the Conference Board's consumer confidence index jumped to one hundred three point three, far above the forecast of about ninety-two, helped by falling gas prices.

36
00:03:39.231 --> 00:03:46.798
Narrator: The ten-year Treasury yield held near four point nine percent, and gold fell more than two and a half percent.

37
00:03:46.798 --> 00:03:53.058
Narrator: The next big number is the P.C.E. inflation report, due today, the day before Thanksgiving.

38
00:03:53.508 --> 00:03:57.505
Narrator: And now for the Microsoft three sixty-five and Entra news.

39
00:03:57.505 --> 00:04:03.156
Narrator: There are two stories you should know about, and the first one is a must-act item.

40
00:04:03.606 --> 00:04:08.032
Narrator: Microsoft has disclosed a data exposure in Entra Connect Health.

41
00:04:08.032 --> 00:04:16.468
Narrator: A flaw in the Connect Health A.P.I., introduced on July twenty-third, let unauthorized parties read tenant-level metadata.

42
00:04:16.468 --> 00:04:25.042
Narrator: That included administrator and technical contact email addresses, tenant IDs, domain names, and sync configuration details.

43
00:04:25.042 --> 00:04:27.808
Narrator: Microsoft says the access was read-only.

44
00:04:27.808 --> 00:04:34.032
Narrator: It found the flaw on November ninth and deployed a server-side fix on November nineteenth.

45
00:04:34.032 --> 00:04:36.590
Narrator: Reports say attackers did exploit it.

46
00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.046
Narrator: Here's why it matters to you.

47
00:04:39.046 --> 00:04:45.201
Narrator: Any client tenant running Entra Connect Health may have had admin contact emails exposed.

48
00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:48.382
Narrator: Those emails are perfect targets for phishing.

49
00:04:48.382 --> 00:04:59.378
Narrator: Check the Message Center and Service Health for each tenant you manage to see whether Microsoft notified you, and warn your admins to expect targeted phishing.

50
00:04:59.378 --> 00:05:03.044
Narrator: Expect lures that mention Microsoft security notices.

51
00:05:03.494 --> 00:05:08.052
Narrator: The second story is the root cause of the November twelfth outage.

52
00:05:08.052 --> 00:05:20.414
Narrator: Microsoft's preliminary post-incident report says the nearly twenty-four-hour outage that took down Exchange Online, Outlook, Teams, and Copilot came from three factors lining up.

53
00:05:20.414 --> 00:05:27.666
Narrator: First, there was a latent lock-contention bug in the networking gateway servers, also introduced in July.

54
00:05:27.666 --> 00:05:31.879
Narrator: Second, Teams traffic failed over onto the Exchange gateways.

55
00:05:31.879 --> 00:05:37.265
Narrator: Third, about fourteen percent of gateway capacity was offline for maintenance.

56
00:05:37.265 --> 00:05:43.895
Narrator: Microsoft says it was not a cyberattack, and no changes are needed on customer Windows machines.

57
00:05:43.895 --> 00:05:48.316
Narrator: If any of your clients asked what happened, this is your answer.

58
00:05:48.766 --> 00:05:58.589
Narrator: Also on the calendar this month, Microsoft is retiring SharePoint one-time passcode authentication for external sharing by the end of November.

59
00:05:58.589 --> 00:06:06.352
Narrator: If any of your clients' external guests still sign in with a passcode, move them to Entra B2B guest accounts now.

60
00:06:06.802 --> 00:06:09.266
Narrator: Now for threats and vulnerabilities.

61
00:06:09.716 --> 00:06:13.504
Narrator: The headline is a breach at U.S. intelligence agencies.

62
00:06:13.504 --> 00:06:23.354
Narrator: The C.I.A. and the Office of the Director of National Intelligence confirmed that an unclassified open-source intelligence system was breached.

63
00:06:23.354 --> 00:06:31.689
Narrator: Officials say no classified information was affected, and a source told the Associated Press the issue has been resolved.

64
00:06:31.689 --> 00:06:40.988
Narrator: The New York Times reported that at least three agencies were affected and that the attackers appear to have used an A.I.-powered tool.

65
00:06:41.438 --> 00:06:46.819
Narrator: On the known exploited vulnerabilities list, CISA added two entries on Monday.

66
00:06:46.819 --> 00:06:51.510
Narrator: Federal agencies must patch both by tomorrow, November twenty-sixth.

67
00:06:51.510 --> 00:07:01.376
Narrator: The first is relevant to the MSP world: a server-side request forgery flaw in N-able Mail Assure, formerly SpamExperts, rated nine point three.

68
00:07:01.376 --> 00:07:06.550
Narrator: If you or any clients use Mail Assure, confirm you're on the patched build.

69
00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:12.689
Narrator: The second is a critical path traversal flaw in MONAI Label, a medical imaging A.I. tool.

70
00:07:12.689 --> 00:07:23.865
Narrator: That one is notable because, according to Amazon threat intelligence, autonomous A.I. agents found and exploited it on their own to take over a university server.

71
00:07:24.315 --> 00:07:32.735
Narrator: Last week, CISA also added actively exploited flaws in VMware vCenter, Cisco Expressway, Apache Roller, and SAP NetWeaver.

72
00:07:32.735 --> 00:07:37.429
Narrator: The vCenter flaw is an authentication bypass rated nine point eight.

73
00:07:37.429 --> 00:07:40.396
Narrator: If you run vCenter anywhere, prioritize it.

74
00:07:40.846 --> 00:07:43.310
Narrator: Moving on to A.I. and local L.L.M.s.

75
00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:48.376
Narrator: November has been one of the busiest months yet for model releases.

76
00:07:48.376 --> 00:07:56.851
Narrator: OpenAI shipped G.P.T. six point two in two versions, Astra and Sol, and cut prices on the flagship by about twenty percent.

77
00:07:56.851 --> 00:08:08.908
Narrator: Google finished its Gemini four lineup with Gemini four Neon, a mid-tier model that's ranking at the top of coding-agent benchmarks for three dollars per million input tokens.

78
00:08:08.908 --> 00:08:16.831
Narrator: Microsoft released MAI Code two, which it says gets close to top-tier coding performance at a fraction of the cost.

79
00:08:16.831 --> 00:08:24.065
Narrator: Earlier in the month, Anthropic released Claude Fable five point two, and Alibaba launched Qwen four Max.

80
00:08:24.515 --> 00:08:30.096
Narrator: On the local hardware side, Nvidia's RTX Spark platform keeps picking up support.

81
00:08:30.096 --> 00:08:40.636
Narrator: The chip pairs a Blackwell G.P.U. with a Grace C.P.U. and up to one hundred twenty-eight gigabytes of unified memory, in slim laptops and small desktops.

82
00:08:40.636 --> 00:08:51.866
Narrator: Nvidia currently recommends models around the thirty-billion-parameter range for local agents, which means you want at least forty-eight gigabytes of total memory.

83
00:08:51.866 --> 00:08:59.030
Narrator: Nvidia's Nemotron three point five Bolt is built specifically for running local agents on this hardware.

84
00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:05.368
Narrator: If you're thinking about your next home lab box, that memory guidance is a useful benchmark.

85
00:09:05.818 --> 00:09:17.708
Narrator: Finally, in big tech, beyond the Nvidia drama, Dell posted record quarterly revenue of fifty-four point nine billion dollars, beating its own forecast on A.I. server demand.

86
00:09:17.708 --> 00:09:29.116
Narrator: Amazon is reportedly buying A.I. optimization technology from Decart for around seven billion dollars, a bet on running models more cheaply on its own Trainium chips.

87
00:09:29.116 --> 00:09:37.912
Narrator: And the Commerce Department moved to stop Chinese companies from renting advanced chips through data centers in other countries.

88
00:09:38.362 --> 00:09:40.787
Narrator: That's your briefing for Wednesday.

89
00:09:40.787 --> 00:09:52.076
Narrator: To recap the action items: check your tenants for an Entra Connect Health notice, patch N-able Mail Assure and vCenter if you run them, and bundle up this morning.

90
00:09:52.076 --> 00:09:54.293
Narrator: Have a great Thanksgiving, Chad.

91
00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:55.470
Narrator: See you tomorrow.
